IMPORT prelude

-- Singapore Labour Foundation Act 1977 (Singapore) -- who the Foundation's bursaries and scholarships are for (s 4(c)), membership:
-- resignation and termination (s 6(4), (5)), the Board: removal of directors, how often it meets, its quorum and casting vote
-- (ss 7, 10), general meetings: the requisition for an extraordinary general meeting, notice, quorum and the adjourned meeting, and
-- virtual meetings hit by a technological disruption (ss 13, 14, 16, 16B), a member's inspection of the records (s 17), what the
-- Foundation may pay to members and directors (s 19), and the protection for acts done in good faith (s 23).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments up to and including 1 December 2021, in operation 31 December 2021),
-- informal consolidation -- version in force from 1/11/2024, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SLFA1977.txt. The latest
-- amendment annotated is Act 30 of 2024 (Platform Workers Act 2024, wef 1 November 2024), which brought platform work associations
-- into s 4; Act 17 of 2023 (wef 1 July 2023) added virtual meeting technology (ss 2, 10(6), 16A, 16B). The arrangement of sections
-- at the top of the deposit is out of step with the body from s 19 onwards (column extraction); the body's numbering is followed.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0211 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. The Act is a constitution for a statutory body, so what it decides for a person is mostly what it decides
-- for a member, a director, a union member's child seeking a bursary, or someone paid by the Foundation.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: incorporation and the common seal (ss 3, 24), the Board's powers (s 5) beyond the committee rule's mention, admission
-- of members (s 6(1)-(3) -- wholly at the Board's discretion), engagement of employees (s 8), the AGM's business (s 12), venue
-- (s 15), the chair and minutes at general meetings (s 16(3), (5)), the mechanics of virtual voting (s 16A), accounts, auditors,
-- shares to the Minister for Finance and the annual report (ss 18, 19A, 20-22), and rules (s 25). No rules made under s 25 were
-- retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Singapore Labour Foundation Act 1977`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` MEANS
    IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `4(c) -- for whom bursaries, scholarships and fellowships are an object`

-- s 4: "The objects of the Foundation are to -- ... (c) provide bursaries, scholarships and fellowships for -- (i) children of members
-- of trade unions and platform work associations affiliated to the National Trades Union Congress and of members of other
-- organisations that are associate affiliates of the National Trades Union Congress; (ii) workers from Singapore or elsewhere who
-- pursue studies or undergo training in Singapore in fields that are relevant to trade unions and platform work associations; and
-- (iii) persons nominated by the National Trades Union Congress to pursue studies in institutions of higher learning in Singapore or
-- elsewhere".
-- This is an OBJECT of the Foundation, not an entitlement: nothing in the Act gives anyone a right to an award. The rule says only
-- whether the person falls within the class s 4(c) names.
DECLARE Applicant IS ONE OF
    `a child of a member of an NTUC-affiliated trade union`
    `a child of a member of an NTUC-affiliated platform work association`
    `a child of a member of an NTUC associate affiliate`
    `a foreign worker training in Singapore in a field relevant to trade unions`
    `a Singapore worker studying abroad in a field relevant to trade unions, not nominated`
    `a person nominated by NTUC to study at a university abroad`
    `a child of a worker in no union`

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant is within the bursary object` IF
    CONSIDER `the applicant`
    WHEN `a Singapore worker studying abroad in a field relevant to trade unions, not nominated` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a child of a worker in no union` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `6(4), (5) -- leaving the Foundation`

-- s 6(4): "A member may resign from the Foundation at any time by giving notice of the member's resignation to the Board, but the
-- member remains liable for any subscription or other sums as may be due to the Foundation on the date of the member's resignation."
-- Sums falling due after the date of resignation are not mentioned; that they are not owed is an INFERENCE.
GIVEN `sums due at the date of resignation` IS A NUMBER, `sums that would fall due afterwards` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`what the resigning member still owes` MEANS
    `sums due at the date of resignation`

-- s 6(5): the Board "may at any time terminate the membership of any member -- (a) if the member has a mental disorder and becomes
-- incapable of managing himself or herself ...; (b) if the member becomes a bankrupt or suspends payment to, or makes any arrangement
-- or composition with, the member's creditors; (c) [a corporate or unincorporated member] becomes insolvent ... or goes into
-- liquidation; (d) if the member fails to pay any annual subscription or other fees due ...; (e) [an NTUC affiliate or associate
-- affiliate] ceases to be so affiliated; (f) if a resolution is passed at a general meeting ...; or (g) for any other reason that to
-- the Board may seem just or proper." Paragraph (g) makes the list illustrative.
GIVEN `the member is mentally incapable` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the member is bankrupt or insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the member failed to pay a subscription or fee` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the member ceased to be NTUC-affiliated` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a general meeting resolved the member should cease` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Board thinks it just or proper` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may terminate the membership` IF
        `the member is mentally incapable`
    OR  `the member is bankrupt or insolvent`
    OR  `the member failed to pay a subscription or fee`
    OR  `the member ceased to be NTUC-affiliated`
    OR  `a general meeting resolved the member should cease`
    OR  `the Board thinks it just or proper`

§§ `7 -- the Board of Directors`

-- s 7(1): the Board consists of "(a) 3 directors to be appointed by the Minister on the advice of the National Trades Union Congress;
-- (b) 2 directors to be appointed by the Minister; and (c) 2 directors to be elected at the annual general meeting". (2) a term of
-- 3 years, eligible for re-appointment. (4): "The Minister may, at any time, revoke any appointment made by him or her under
-- subsection (1)(a) or (b) without giving any reason; and any director elected under subsection (1)(c) may be removed by a resolution
-- passed at a general meeting".
DECLARE Director IS ONE OF
    `a director appointed on NTUC advice`
    `a director appointed by the Minister`
    `an elected director`

GIVEN `the director` IS A Director
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may remove the director without reason` IF
    CONSIDER `the director`
    WHEN `an elected director` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the director` IS A Director
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a general meeting may remove the director` IF
    CONSIDER `the director`
    WHEN `an elected director` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `10 -- meetings of the Board`

-- s 10(1): the Chairperson must summon Board meetings "as often as may be necessary but not less frequently than once in 3 months".
GIVEN `months since the last Board meeting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board is meeting often enough` IF
    `months since the last Board meeting` AT MOST 3

-- s 10(2): "At every meeting of the Board, 4 directors form a quorum, and decisions are to be adopted by a simple majority of the
-- votes of the directors present and voting, except in the case of an equality of votes when the Chairperson, or the person presiding
-- at the meeting, has a casting vote." (5): a vacancy does not stop the Board acting, "Subject to subsection (2)".
GIVEN `directors present` IS A NUMBER, `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER, `the presiding director casts for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board adopts the decision` IF
        `directors present` AT LEAST 4
    AND (    `votes for` GREATER THAN `votes against`
         OR  (`votes for` EQUALS `votes against` AND `the presiding director casts for`))

§§ `13 -- requisitioning an extraordinary general meeting`

-- s 13(1): "Upon receipt of a requisition in writing by at least 100 members or one-quarter of the total number of members, whichever
-- is less, the Secretary to the Board must forthwith convene an extraordinary general meeting". (2): the requisition "must state the
-- objects of the meeting and must be signed by the requisitionists and deposited at the office of the Foundation".
GIVEN `total members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the requisition threshold` MEANS
    `the smaller of` 100 (`total members` DIVIDED BY 4)

GIVEN `total members` IS A NUMBER, `signatories` IS A NUMBER, `states the objects` IS A BOOLEAN, `deposited at the office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Secretary must convene an extraordinary general meeting` IF
        `signatories` AT LEAST `the requisition threshold` `total members`
    AND `states the objects`
    AND `deposited at the office`

§§ `14 -- notice of a general meeting`

-- s 14(1): the Board must send notice of every general meeting "at least 14 days prior to the meeting being held", specifying "the
-- date, time and place ..., the nature of the business ... and, in case of special business, concise particulars". (2): "The
-- accidental omission to give the notice to, and the non-receipt of the notice by, a member does not invalidate the proceedings".
-- Whether "14 days prior" counts clear days is not said; the rule counts the days between sending and the meeting (an INFERENCE).
GIVEN `days between notice and meeting` IS A NUMBER, `states date, time, place and business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice complies with s 14(1)` IF
        `days between notice and meeting` AT LEAST 14
    AND `states date, time, place and business`

§§ `16 -- quorum at a general meeting`

-- s 16(1): "One-quarter of the total number of members of the Foundation as recorded in the register of members forms a quorum".
-- (2): if no quorum within half an hour, the meeting "stands adjourned to the same day in the next week at the same place and time;
-- and if, at the adjourned meeting, a quorum is not present within half an hour ..., the persons entitled to vote who are present
-- constitute a quorum". That at least one voter must be present is an INFERENCE.
GIVEN `members on the register` IS A NUMBER, `voters present` IS A NUMBER, `this is the adjourned meeting after half an hour` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the general meeting is quorate` IF
        `voters present` AT LEAST `members on the register` DIVIDED BY 4
    OR  (`this is the adjourned meeting after half an hour` AND `voters present` AT LEAST 1)

§§ `16B -- a virtual meeting hit by a technological disruption`

-- s 16B: "A meeting to which section 16A(2)(b) or (c) applies [physical and virtual, or virtual only] is not invalidated by reason of
-- any technological disruption, malfunction or outage unless the court -- (a) is of the opinion that the technological disruption ...
-- has caused or may cause substantial injustice that cannot be remedied by any order of the court; and (b) by order declares the
-- meeting to be invalid." For a wholly physical meeting s 16B does not apply, and the rule returns FALSE (the saving is not engaged).
GIVEN `the meeting used virtual meeting technology` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the court finds irremediable substantial injustice` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the court declares the meeting invalid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 16B saves the meeting despite the disruption` IF
        `the meeting used virtual meeting technology`
    AND (NOT (`the court finds irremediable substantial injustice` AND `the court declares the meeting invalid`))

§§ `17 -- inspecting the register, minutes and books`

-- s 17: the register of members, minutes and books of account "must, subject to any rules that may be in force, be open to inspection
-- by members, provided that the written permission of the Chairperson or of a director is obtained prior to the inspection".
GIVEN `the person is a member` IS A BOOLEAN, `has prior written permission of the Chairperson or a director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may inspect the records` IF
    `the person is a member` AND `has prior written permission of the Chairperson or a director`

§§ `19 -- what may be paid to members, directors and others`

-- s 19(1): income and property "must be applied solely towards the promotion of the objects ... and no portion ... may be paid or
-- transferred directly or indirectly by way of dividend, bonus, profit or otherwise to members or directors". (2): this does not
-- prevent "the payment, in good faith, of -- (a) remuneration to employees ...; (b) remuneration to the director charged with general
-- administrative control over the work of the Foundation as provided in section 9; (c) out-of-pocket and travelling expenses to any
-- director; and (d) other proper charges and expenses". Treating a fee to an ordinary director as outside (d) is an INFERENCE from
-- (b) naming only the s 9 director; s 9 also allows that director's appointment to be honorary.
DECLARE Payment IS ONE OF
    `a dividend to members`
    `a bonus to a director`
    `a salary to an employee`
    `remuneration to the director in general administrative control`
    `travelling expenses to a director`
    `a fee to an ordinary director for serving on the Board`

GIVEN `the payment` IS A Payment, `made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Foundation may make the payment` IF
        `made in good faith`
    AND CONSIDER `the payment`
        WHEN `a salary to an employee` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `remuneration to the director in general administrative control` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `travelling expenses to a director` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `23 -- protection from liability`

-- s 23: nothing done by "any director or member or by any employee engaged by the Board shall, if the matter or thing was done ...
-- bona fide for the purpose of carrying out the provisions of this Act, subject any such director, member or employee to any action,
-- liability, claim or demand whatsoever".
GIVEN `acted bona fide` IS A BOOLEAN, `for the purpose of carrying out the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the director, member or employee is protected` IF
    `acted bona fide` AND `for the purpose of carrying out the Act`
